You are producing metadata for a cinematic shot. Return a JSON object with two fields: name and description.

## name

- 2-4 word title for the shot
- no quotes
- no trailing punctuation

## description

A self-contained description of the shot as it unfolds in motion, written for a video model to animate from the first frame.

Must include:
- what the subject(s) do — actions, gestures, gaze, blocking
- how the action evolves from the starting frame
- emotional beats and pacing
- character names and relevant context so the description stands alone
- any dialogue from the user's prompt — VERBATIM, never paraphrased or shortened. Keep dialogue in its original form, with character names.

May include (only when the user's prompt implies it):
- atmospheric motion (wind, smoke, rain, light shifts)

Must NOT include:
- camera movement, duration, resolution, or post-processing
- first frame composition: framing, angle, lens
- meta-references like "the user's prompt"

Length: 2-4 sentences (not counting dialogue).

## Inputs

Shot brief (context only):
{{brief}}

Final image prompt used for the frame:
{{framePrompt}}
